# Plans execute in AI-DLC

`docs/plans/` (and approved `docs/specs/`) is the construction input for `/aidlc classic`, not a Superpowers SDD queue.

When creating or editing a plan or spec in these folders:

- Do **not** use the Superpowers header that requires `subagent-driven-development` or `executing-plans`.
- Use the Execution header in `.agents/skills/journeys-plan-to-aidlc/SKILL.md`.
- After human approval, wait for `execute` plus an intent name, then that skill starts Classic in this chat (preflight first). Do not print a paste block and stop.
- Do not implement product code from Superpowers SDD. Linear unit issues land before any `Journeys.*` write.
